<section class="access-section section-frame" id="network">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <h2>One terminal.<br />Every leg connected.</h2>
    <p>For traders, bin builders, and developers composing positions across Hyperliquid's markets.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="access-columns">
    <article>
      <span class="small-label">BIN AND STRATEGY BUILDERS</span>
      <h3>Bring a narrative or a rule.<br />Let others follow it.</h3>
      <p>Group markets around a narrative or write a rule-based strategy, publish the reasoning behind it, and let verified users follow it from the leaderboard.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="#assets">Explore the bins <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </article>
    <article>
      <span class="small-label">DEVELOPER INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
      <h3>Read the same markets.<br />Keep your own keys.</h3>
      <p>Every bin is built from Hyperliquid's public market data, so each leg, weight and price is visible before you enter. OpenCash never receives a private key.</p>
      <details>
        <summary>View integration overview <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary>
        <div class="integration-details">
          <p>Market data is read from Hyperliquid's public API. Orders are signed by a trade-only key and sized to the market's lot step before they are sent.</p>
          <code>loadMarkets()<br />sizeBinFor(bin, margin, data)<br />openBin(trader, sized, data, onStep)<br />loadOpenPositions(owner, data)<br />closePosition(trader, position)</code>
          <p>The trading key cannot withdraw, and every order runs on Hyperliquid testnet during early access.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>
